course: dictionary
lesson: 6385
title: Multilingual
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Multilingual means able to speak or use several languages. The word starts with multi-, which means many, so multilingual means many languages.
explain: «Many people in the world grow up bilingual (speaking two languages) or multilingual (speaking several).» The brackets give you the clues: bilingual is two languages, and multilingual is several, which means more than two.
explain: Multilingual can describe a person or a thing. A multilingual child speaks more than one language, and a multilingual sign is written in several languages. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "Many children are able to speak several languages" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Multilingual means able to speak or use several languages.
fact: Bilingual means two languages; multilingual means several, which is more than two.
fact: A multilingual sign, dictionary or school uses several languages.
fact: Airports, museums and hospitals often use multilingual signs so that visitors can understand them.
fact: Multilingual is an adjective. A multilingual is a rare noun for a person who speaks several languages.
exercise: «Many people in the world grow up bilingual or multilingual.» What does multilingual mean? | Speaking only one language | Able to sing very well | *Speaking several languages | Speaking no words at all
exercise: An airport sign says "Exit" in English, French, Arabic and Hindi. What kind of sign is it? | A sign with only pictures | *A multilingual sign | A very old sign | A sign written in one language only
exercise: Which word means speaking two languages? | Dangerous | *Bilingual | Glowing | Multilingual
test: A multilingual family speaks Polish at home and English at school. How many languages do they use? | No language at all | *Several languages | One language | Only sign language
test: What does a multilingual school mean? | *A school where several languages are used | A school with only one class | A school that closes early | A school with no books
exam: Which sentence uses multilingual correctly? | The bread was multilingual this morning. | *The airport has multilingual signs in six languages. | My pencil is very multilingual. | She ran multilingual across the field.
